  "summary": "Experienced Network & Software Test Engineer with a demonstrated history of working in the wireless industry. Good understanding on 4G & 5G concepts such as DL/UL scheduling, LTE power control, Beamforming fundamentals, MIMO, ENDC. Good Understanding on 5G networks SA & NSA, mmWave& Sub6. Performed 5G testing on NR Bands (mmW n261/n260/n258, Mid n25, n66, n41, Low n71). Strong knowledge on 4G& 5G air interface and call processing technologies and network architecture specifically focused on Radio Access Network. Good understanding of overall Wireless systems with emphasis on PHY, MAC, RLC, RRC and PDCP layers. Good knowledge of cellular (5N NR, LTE-A/LTE, and Wi-Fi advanced) PHY/MAC and upper layers. Experience with QXDM, and Android SDK logging tools. Skilled in Universal Mobile Telecommunications System (UMTS,CDMA,LTE), Test Planning, Telecommunications, Testing, and Agilent 8960. Strong network & software professional with a Master of Business Administration and Master's in Computer Science from Monroe College.",
