    "description": "QCT Modem Field Test Engineer\n•\tWork with a multidiscipline team (Software Development, System Design, Customer Support, ASIC Design, RF Circuits and Hardware Design, etc.) to test and commercialize QCT products. \n•\tResponsible for conducting drive tests, troubleshooting/analyzing problems, optimizing system performance and supporting Qualcomm’s customers with product commercialization. \n•\tResponsible for performing lab testing and drive testing for ATT, TMO, VZ and Sprint sites supporting RF network design and optimization, measuring and mapping RF signal strength levels in tristate area, modeling RF propagation, analyzing multi-transmitter communication networks under highly competitive atmosphere with strict deadlines \n•\tResponsible for reproducing and resolving LTE and VOLTE issues from test scenarios on field such as Throughput, Mobility, Carrier Aggregation, Conference CSFB calls and SRVCC in NJ/NY market with different Infrastructure like Alcatel Lucent and Ericsson.\n•\tDebugging RACH issues on commercial OTA network and thorough layer to layer analysis of cell reselection, Handovers, RLFs, SIB-Read Failures, OOS and IRAT by parsing collected QXDM logs in APEX to validate access failures\n•\tProvisioning various MSM/MDM chipsets for LTE and VOLTE using J-TAG for Sanity and Regression testing with different network carriers. \n•\tPreparing reports with results for tests, location, device information, observation and issues.\n",
